    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>About This Game</strong><br><i>Xiao Jun (English Edition)</i> is a hand-drawn, story-driven 2D RPG set in 1990s China. It tells the full life journey of a rural boy \u2014 from bullied schoolchild, to a Bitcoin millionaire, and ultimately a tragic rebel against a corrupt system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game where <strong>story comes first</strong>, but it includes <strong>light turn-based combat</strong> during key moments of tension. Battles are few, but emotionally significant.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83e\udde8 A Life Shaped by Injustice, Greed, and Memory</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Childhood</strong>: Face bullies, suffer loss, and grow up in a harsh rural society.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Youth</strong>: Build friendships, experience betrayal, and dream of escape.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Collapse &amp; Fortune</strong>: Discover forgotten Bitcoin and gain sudden wealth.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rebellion</strong>: Build a mining empire \u2014 and clash with the village, the system, and yourself.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Final Stand</strong>: An explosive ending that confronts the cost of power and resistance.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83c\udfae Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Narrative-Focused RPG</strong>: A mostly linear experience with <strong>occasional turn-based battles</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-Drawn Visuals</strong>: Rich illustrations of 1990s China\u2019s rural and urban life.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Emotional Storytelling</strong>: A story about pain, memory, and revenge \u2014 told over decades.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Cultural Depth</strong>: Social realism rarely seen in RPGs, set in contemporary China.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83d\udd52 Playtime:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Around <strong>3 to 4 hours</strong> to complete the full story.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you enjoy games like <i>To the Moon</i>, <i>Detention</i>, or <i>Rakuen</i>, this game will leave a lasting emotional impression \u2014 with just enough challenge to feel the stakes.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>About This Game</strong><br><i>Xiao Jun (English Edition)</i> is a hand-drawn, story-driven 2D RPG set in 1990s China. It tells the full life journey of a rural boy \u2014 from bullied schoolchild, to a Bitcoin millionaire, and ultimately a tragic rebel against a corrupt system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a game where <strong>story comes first</strong>, but it includes <strong>light turn-based combat</strong> during key moments of tension. Battles are few, but emotionally significant.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83e\udde8 A Life Shaped by Injustice, Greed, and Memory</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Childhood</strong>: Face bullies, suffer loss, and grow up in a harsh rural society.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Youth</strong>: Build friendships, experience betrayal, and dream of escape.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Collapse &amp; Fortune</strong>: Discover forgotten Bitcoin and gain sudden wealth.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Rebellion</strong>: Build a mining empire \u2014 and clash with the village, the system, and yourself.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Final Stand</strong>: An explosive ending that confronts the cost of power and resistance.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83c\udfae Key Features:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Narrative-Focused RPG</strong>: A mostly linear experience with <strong>occasional turn-based battles</strong>.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hand-Drawn Visuals</strong>: Rich illustrations of 1990s China\u2019s rural and urban life.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Emotional Storytelling</strong>: A story about pain, memory, and revenge \u2014 told over decades.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Cultural Depth</strong>: Social realism rarely seen in RPGs, set in contemporary China.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >\ud83d\udd52 Playtime:</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Around <strong>3 to 4 hours</strong> to complete the full story.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you enjoy games like <i>To the Moon</i>, <i>Detention</i>, or <i>Rakuen</i>, this game will leave a lasting emotional impression \u2014 with just enough challenge to feel the stakes.</p>",
